      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so when you say the dissent is \"viewed as legally flawed,\" are you saying that their legal reasoning is actually incorrect within the framework of constitutional law, or just that it disagrees with the majority's interpretation? basically, is there a consensus among legal scholars that the dissent's logic doesn't hold up?",
